-- Nothing a request commits may depend on NOTIFY. Postgres has ONE notification queue for the whole
-- cluster (8 GB by default, and as many pg_notify files on disk) and no privilege for LISTEN or
-- NOTIFY: a login role that LISTENs and then stops reading its socket, or stays inside a transaction,
-- keeps the queue from being emptied, and a second session that sends notifications fills it in
-- minutes. From then on EVERY transaction that notified fails with 54000 ("too many notifications in
-- the NOTIFY queue") at COMMIT, a code that exception blocks inside a function do not catch. Since
-- 0047 auth_otp_issue notified for every accepted request, so the day the queue was full no OTP could
-- be issued for any tenant (login, signup, invite, reset, phone change), and the admin outbox insert
-- failed with its audit row. Password login was unaffected, which is what made it a denial of one
-- path by any compromised role (the shape of db-r14-3, reached through shared server state that no
-- ACL can close).
